    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0610" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg568"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 16, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 8th instant, communicating an authenticated copy of
                    a protest made by the master, mate, and steward of the British steamer
                    Peterhoff, before the British vice-consul at Key West, and also an authenticated
                    extract from the official log of the ship.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to inform you that a copy of these papers has been
                    communicated to the attorney of the United States for the southern district of
                    New York, for his information.</p>
                <pb facs="0611" n="569" xml:id="pg569"/>
                <p>The documents which accompanied your note are herewith returned to you, in
                    conformity with your request.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, your very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
